'' =============================================================================
''
''   File....... test-vo-f372-usb-wrpin-on-running-pair.spin2
''   Purpose.... VO-F372 on SILICON: in USB mode %11011, does a new WRPIN on a RUNNING pair (DIR high) change
''               drive <-> sniffer cleanly, or does it need a reset (DIR cycle)?
''   Authors.... Iron Sheep Productions, LLC
''   E-mail..... stephen@ironsheep.biz
''   Started.... Oct 2026
''   Updated.... Oct 2026
''
'' =============================================================================

{ WHAT IS DECIDED  (register VO-F372; close-out study step 8; bench-groupD-recheck.md section 4.2)

  The sources disagree by edition about changing a running USB pair with a new WRPIN:
    SAYS YES   p2-hardware-manual-text.txt:1488 "Using D data of %0_11011_0 will disable output drive and effectively create a USB
               'sniffer'. A new WRPIN can be done to effect such a change without resetting the smart pin."  The same sentence is at
               smart-pins-titus-text.txt:1381-1382 and silicon-doc/p2-documentation.txt:8885-8886.
    OMITS IT   silicon-doc-text.txt:4579 (the newest capture) gives the sniffer sentence without it; :4581 allows only WXPIN
               ("these settings can be changed on-the-fly without resetting the USB smart pins").
    OPPOSITE   silicon-doc-text.txt:3856: "You could do a WRPIN while DIR is high, but the unregulated change in use of the 126 state
               bits would cause unpredictable and quite certainly useless behavior" -- written about changing the five %SSSSS mode bits;
               a same-mode TT change keeps %11011, so reading it as covering this case is an inference.
    Working code (usbnew.spin2) always raises DIRL before WRPIN: silent.  EF-012 shows only that a WRPIN on a running pin is accepted.
  This program asks: does WRPIN %0_11011_0 / %1_11011_0 on a running pair give the same line behaviour as the documented reset-based
  reconfigure (DIRL, WRPIN, WXPIN, DIRH), and is the pair still intact afterwards (a framed packet round-trips)?

  RIG  (BARE BOARD -- NOTHING ATTACHED)
    One USB pair: P0 = DM (even, the lower pin) and P1 = DP (odd).  "The receiver receives not just input from another host/device,
    but all local output, as well" (silicon-doc-text.txt:4614) -- so the pair reads its own output and no second pair and no jumper
    is needed.  P0 and P1 are driven by the program (full-speed host, 12 Mbps) -- attach NOTHING to them.
    SELF-SENSE WITHOUT THE 1.5k / 15k RESISTORS MAY BE AMBIGUOUS (a bare, floating pair; a sniffer pad can retain the last level it was
    driven to).  This program is the self-sense form ONLY; it does not contain the jumpered arm.  The FALLBACK, to be built as a separate
    test only if this run comes back INCONCLUSIVE for that reason (the INCONCLUSIVE lines say so), is the recheck's: a second USB pair
    P2/P3 and two jumpers P0->P2 and P1->P3 (the second pair is the sniffer, a distinct receiver).  Pins P2/P3 are NOT used here.
    Floating-pad defence in this program: the sniffer step writes J (WYPIN #3) and the back-to-drive step writes K (WYPIN #2), and
    back-to-drive is accepted only when it reads exactly K (%010); a pad that merely retained J cannot pass it.

  DEBUGGER (EF-057)
    DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001: the debug interrupt lives in cog 0 only.  Every pin operation runs in a dedicated PASM cog started by
    COGINIT; it writes results to a hub mailbox; cog 0 reports.  Every printed line is built in a hub buffer and sent by ONE debug()
    record.  Compile with pnut-ts -d; nothing on P62.

  CONFIGURATION WORDS, FIELD BY FIELD (WRPIN D = %AAAA_BBBB_FFF_MMMMMMMMMMMMM_TT_SSSSS_0, silicon-doc-text.txt:3731; %SSSSS list :3807-:3841;
  USB text :4579-:4593; Spin2 symbols spin2-v55-text.txt:1521-:1526, :1557)
    drive   $0000_0076  AAAA=0000 BBBB=0000 FFF=000 M=0 TT=%01 SSSSS=%11011 bit0=0   = P_USB_PAIR | P_OE   (D data %1_11011_0, :4579)
    sniffer $0000_0036  AAAA=0000 BBBB=0000 FFF=000 M=0 TT=%00 SSSSS=%11011 bit0=0   = P_USB_PAIR          (D data %0_11011_0, :4579)
    TT bit 0 = output enable for all smart modes (:3795-:3797: "x0 = output disabled, regardless of DIR / x1 = output enabled").
    WXPIN on the lower pin (:4583-:4587): D[15] = 1 host, D[14] = 1 full-speed, D[13:0] = (12_000_000 FRAC clkfreq) >> 16 = $0F5C = 3932
    at 200 MHz  ->  $CF5C.  Cog 0 recomputes the baud with the Spin2 FRAC operator at run time and gates on it (control W).
    Pair addressing: PAIR = DM | (1 << 6) = 64 -- S[10:6] = 1 additional pin, as the documentation's "bothpins" (:4595, and the WRPIN /
    DIRH ADDPINS form used at :4424).

  STATUS WORD (lower pin, silicon-doc-text.txt:4618-:4629): [2] SE0 in, [1] K in, [0] J in, [3] steady state, [4] SOP in, [5] EOP in,
    [6] error, [7] byte toggle (cleared on SOP, toggled on each byte), [15:8] last byte.  WYPIN codes (:4597-:4605): 2 = K, 3 = J,
    $80 = SOP then data bytes.  A "SNAPSHOT" below = SETTLE_CLK clocks of settling, then SAMPLES quiet reads (RQPIN) of the status word,
    SPACE_CLK clocks apart; SEEN = the OR of (status AND %111) over the samples (which of SE0/K/J were ever seen), LAST = the last word.

  SEQUENCE (the measuring cog; ROUNDS rounds; every pin operation here)
    LIVE ARM
      start   DIRL pair, WRPIN #0 pair, WRPIN drive pair, WXPIN host+FS+baud on DM, DIRH pair, wait         (the documented start, :4593)
      (1) CONTROL  WYPIN #2 (K), snapshot -> must be SEEN = %010 ;  WYPIN #3 (J), snapshot -> must be SEEN = %001 ;
                   framed packet: SOP, $A5, $5A, $3C, $C3, read back through the status word (byte toggle) -> must return the 4 bytes
      (2) LIVE TO SNIFFER, DIR high   WRPIN sniffer pair (no DIR change, no WXPIN) ; snapshot (no write) ; WYPIN #3 (J) ; snapshot
      (3) LIVE BACK TO DRIVE, DIR high   WRPIN drive pair ; snapshot ; WYPIN #2 (K) ; snapshot
      (4) PACKET after the live changes (WYPIN #3 back to idle J first, so it starts from the control's state): the same framed packet as in (1)
          characterization only (not in the verdict): WXPIN host+FS+baud re-issued on DM, then the packet again -- if (4) fails and
          this passes, the live WRPIN lost the WXPIN settings
    DIR-CYCLE ARM (what a reset-based reconfigure gives; the reference)
      start (as above) ; DIRL pair, WRPIN sniffer pair, WXPIN, DIRH pair ; WYPIN #3 (J) ; snapshot
                       ; DIRL pair, WRPIN drive pair, WXPIN, DIRH pair   ; WYPIN #2 (K) ; snapshot
    After the last round the control arm (1) is run once more (control after).

  CONTROLS (gating -- a failure prints RIG FAIL and NO VERDICT)
    W : the configuration words decode to the fields above and equal their Spin2 symbol compositions; the baud word equals the FRAC
        computation; DM is even, DP = DM + 1, both in the free set.
    K : the control arm (1), every round AND once after the rounds: K snapshot SEEN = %010, J snapshot SEEN = %001.  (Proves the pair is
        driving and that the receiver sees its own output.)
    R : DIR-cycle arm: the "back to drive" snapshot SEEN = %010 (K) in every round (the documented reconfigure restores the drive and
        the WYPIN #2 after it is seen).
    O : DIR-cycle arm: the sniffer snapshot SEEN is the same in every round AND does not contain K (%010 clear) -- the sniffer is observable.
        If not, nothing separates "drive" from "sniffer": INCONCLUSIVE (never a pass).
    B : DIR-cycle arm: the sniffer snapshot SEEN is never exactly J (%001) in any round.  A sniffer that reads J-only is
        indistinguishable from a pad that retained the J of the sniffer step's WYPIN #3, so it is not an independent receiver: if B fails
        the BACK arm is INCONCLUSIVE (the sniffer arm and the packet arm may still decide BREAKS).
    P : the control packet returned all 4 bytes in every round.  If not, the packet arm (4) is printed as characterization and does not
        enter the verdict (the verdict then rests on (2) and (3), and its line ends "(packet arm excluded)").
    T : the measuring cog reports done within RIG_TIMEOUT_SEC = 5 s (clkfreq x 5 = 1.0e9 stays below 2^31 = 2.147e9).

  PRE-REGISTERED OUTCOMES (fixed before the run; printed by the program)
    SNIFF_OK   : every round, the live-to-sniffer SEEN (after WYPIN #3) equals the DIR-cycle sniffer SEEN.
    SNIFF_BAD  : in every round it differs.
    BACK_OK    : every round, the live-back SEEN (after WYPIN #2) equals %010 (K) -- the same as the DIR-cycle arm.  A pad that merely
                 retained J reads %001 and fails this.
    BACK_BAD   : in every round it differs.
    PKT_OK     : (gate P holding) every round, the packet after the live changes returns the same bytes as the control packet.
    PKT_BAD    : (gate P holding) in every round it does not.
    SURVIVES (the hardware manual / Titus / old Silicon Doc are right): SNIFF_OK and BACK_OK, and PKT_OK when gate P holds.
    BREAKS   (the Silicon Doc 'unpredictable' reading is right for this case): SNIFF_BAD or BACK_BAD or PKT_BAD.
    INCONCLUSIVE : anything else (mixed rounds), or the control arm / observability gates do not hold.  Every INCONCLUSIVE line names the
                 fallback: a second pair with jumpers P0->P2 and P1->P3 (not part of this program).
    The line states after each live WRPIN with no WYPIN (the 'snapshot (no write)') are printed as characterization only.

  DEVIATIONS FROM THE BRIEF (bench-groupD-recheck.md section 4.2)
    1. Arm (2) writes WYPIN #3 (J) and arm (3) writes WYPIN #2 (K) (the brief has #2 in both).  Before the sniffer step the transmitter's
       last-set state is J (the control's last WYPIN #3); a floating sniffer pad that retains J would read J, so "back to drive" is
       accepted only when it reads K, a level only the new drive WYPIN can produce.  The DIR-cycle reference uses the same two values.
    2. Each observation is a SNAPSHOT of 8 reads (the OR of the line-state bits), not one read of "bit 1", so a line that flickers
       (a floating sniffer) is seen as such instead of passing on one lucky read.  A sniffer's absolute state is not predicted: the sniffer
       is compared with the DIR-cycle sniffer, not with a value.
    3. The control arm is repeated before every live arm (every round) and once after the rounds.
    4. The packet is read back through the receiver's byte toggle with a PASM polling loop (about 20 clocks per poll against 133 clocks per
       byte at 12 Mbps).  The brief says "verify the status word's bytes".

  VERIFIED OPCODES AND DATA (pnut-ts -d -l v1.55.8 build 9/19/2026, read from the .lst; object offsets, cog addresses in brackets)
    Symbol table (listing): CFG_DRIVE = SYM_DRIVE = $0000_0076, CFG_SNIFF = SYM_SNIFF = $0000_0036, USB_HOST_FS = $C000,
      USB_BAUD = $0F5C, X_USB = $0000_CF5C, PAIR = $40, RECW = $22 (34), MB_RES = $02, MB_POST = $AC, MB_LONGS = $B6 ;
      record slots LX_N = $18 .. LX_EOP = $1D, DS_SEEN = $1E.  CLKMODE $010009FB, CLKFREQ 200_000_000, XINFREQ 20_000_000 (listing).
    DEBUG: 2 records, 24 bytes of DEBUG data.  Engine at object offset $054; cog labels: usb_off [$02E] usb_start [$033] usb_cycle
      [$034] control_arm [$03B] snap [$041] packet [$050] put [$090] cfg_drive_ [$093] x_usb_ [$095] txdata_ [$097]; registers cfg_ [$0A1],
      seen_ [$0A2], st_ [$0A4], val_ [$0A6], nrx_ [$0A7], txi_ [$0A8], insop_ [$0A9], prevtg_ [$0AA], rx0_..rx3_ [$0AB..$0AE],
      b_ [$0AF], eop_ [$0B0]; the cog image ends at $0B3 (self_id_).
    Instructions read back from the hub image (the .bin; object base = bin offset 9242, engine = base + $54; condition IF_C = $C,
    IF_C_AND_Z = $8, IF_NC = $3, IF_Z = $A in bits 31:28):
      dirl #PAIR $FD648040   dirh #PAIR $FD648041   outl #PAIR $FD648048   wrpin #0,#PAIR $FC0C0040   waitx #100 $FD64C81F
      wrpin cfg_,#PAIR $FC054240 (D=$0A1, S=64)   wxpin x_usb_,#PIN_DM $FC152A00 (D=$095, S=0)   ret $FD64002D
      wypin #2,#PAIR $FC2C0440   wypin #3,#PAIR $FC2C0640   rqpin st_,#PIN_DM $FA854800   testp #PIN_DP wc $FD740240
      cmp txi_,#NTX wc $F2155005   alts txi_,#txdata_ $F9955097   wypin b_,#PAIR $FC255E40   testb st_,#4 wc $F4154804
      cmp insop_,#0 wz $F20D5200   if_z_and_c mov insop_,#1 $86055201   altd nrx_,#rx0_ / if_c mov 0-0,b_ $C98D4EAB / $C60000AF
    The round body, read back in order: wrpin cfg_sniff_ $FC052840 / call snap / wypin #3 / call snap / wrpin cfg_drive_ $FC052640 /
      call snap / wypin #2 / call snap / NEW: wypin #3 + waitx ##SETTLE_CLK ($FF800007 $FD67401F) / call packet / NEW: wxpin x_usb_,#PIN_DM
      $FC152A00 + waitx ##START_CLK ($FF800027 $FD64401F) / call packet; then the DIR-cycle arm: wypin #3 then #2 ($FC2C0640, $FC2C0440).

  HOW TO RUN
    1. USB serial connected (DEBUG on P62/P63).  Compile: pnut-ts -d test-vo-f372-usb-wrpin-on-running-pair.spin2
    2. Load to RAM with DEBUG enabled (pnut-term-ts, or PNut Ctrl-F10).
    3. SAVE THE WHOLE CONSOLE OUTPUT -- it is the only record.
    4. Expected run time: the engine about 100 ms (5 rounds), the report about 80 lines.  Done when you see one "VERDICT VO-F372: ..." line
       (or "NO VERDICT"), then "=== END ===" and DEBUG_END_SESSION.  No END / DEBUG_END_SESSION line within 15 s = a hang or a lost
       session: power-cycle the board and send the LAST line you saw.
    5. Clock: _clkfreq = 200_000_000 assumes the board's 20 MHz crystal; the listing's CLKMODE is quoted in the VERIFIED block above.  The
       12 Mbps baud word is computed from clkfreq, so another crystal changes the line rate too.
    6. Pins: P0 (DM) and P1 (DP) are DRIVEN by the program as a USB host pair.  NOTHING may be attached to P0 or P1 (no jumper, no
       resistor, no scope load that you cannot lose).  No other pin is touched.  (P2 / P3 are used only by the fallback described in the
       RIG section, which is not part of this program.)
}

CON ' ---- Rig Parameters ----
  _clkfreq          = 200_000_000
  DEBUG_COGS        = %0000_0001        ' EF-057: debugger in cog 0 ONLY

  PIN_DM            = 0                 ' lower (even) pin of the pair
  PIN_DP            = PIN_DM + 1        ' upper (odd) pin
  PAIR              = PIN_DM | (1 << 6) ' DM plus one additional pin (S[10:6] = 1)
  PIN_MAX_FREE_LOW  = 7                 ' free set: P0..P7 and P32..P47

  ROUNDS            = 5
  SAMPLES           = 8                 ' quiet status reads per snapshot
  SPACE_CLK         = 400               ' clocks between the reads of a snapshot
  SETTLE_CLK        = 4_000             ' clocks of settling before a snapshot (240 bit periods)
  START_CLK         = 20_000            ' clocks after a start (DIRH) before the first write
  PKT_TIMEOUT       = 1_000_000         ' clocks for a packet to complete (5 ms)
  RIG_TIMEOUT_SEC   = 5
  MBOX_DONE         = 1
  NO_BYTE           = $FFFF_FFFF        ' a received-byte slot that never filled

  USB_HOST_FS       = $C000             ' D[15] = 1 host, D[14] = 1 full-speed
  USB_BAUD          = $0F5C             ' (12_000_000 FRAC 200_000_000) >> 16 = 3932
  X_USB             = USB_HOST_FS | USB_BAUD

  SEEN_J            = %001              ' status bit 0 = J in
  SEEN_K            = %010              ' status bit 1 = K in
  NBYTES            = 4                 ' data bytes of the framed packet (after SOP)
  NTX               = NBYTES + 1        ' values written: SOP then the data
  TX0               = $A5
  TX1               = $5A
  TX2               = $3C
  TX3               = $C3

CON ' ---- Configuration Words ----
  CFG_DRIVE         = $0000_0076        ' P_USB_PAIR | P_OE  (D data %1_11011_0)
  CFG_SNIFF         = $0000_0036        ' P_USB_PAIR         (D data %0_11011_0)
  SYM_DRIVE         = P_USB_PAIR | P_OE
  SYM_SNIFF         = P_USB_PAIR

  ' WRPIN D field positions and widths (silicon-doc-text.txt:3731)
  SHIFT_AAAA        = 28
  MASK_AAAA         = %1111
  SHIFT_BBBB        = 24
  MASK_BBBB         = %1111
  SHIFT_FFF         = 21
  MASK_FFF          = %111
  SHIFT_M           = 8
  MASK_M            = %1_1111_1111_1111
  SHIFT_TT          = 6
  MASK_TT           = %11
  SHIFT_SSSSS       = 1
  MASK_SSSSS        = %1_1111
  MASK_BIT0         = 1
  SSSSS_USB         = %11011
  TT_OFF            = %00
  TT_ON             = %01

CON ' ---- Mailbox Layout ----
  ' per round record (RECW longs), written by the engine in this order:
  '  CK_SEEN, CK_LAST        control K snapshot
  '  CJ_SEEN, CJ_LAST        control J snapshot
  '  CP_N, CP_B0..CP_B3, CP_EOP   control packet: bytes received, the four bytes, EOP-in seen
  '  LS0_SEEN, LS0_LAST      after the live WRPIN to sniffer, no write
  '  LS_SEEN, LS_LAST        live sniffer after WYPIN #3 (J)
  '  LB0_SEEN, LB0_LAST      after the live WRPIN back to drive, no write
  '  LB_SEEN, LB_LAST        live back after WYPIN #2 (K)
  '  LP_N, LP_B0..LP_B3, LP_EOP   packet after the live changes
  '  DS_SEEN, DS_LAST        DIR-cycle sniffer after WYPIN #3 (J)
  '  DB_SEEN, DB_LAST        DIR-cycle back after WYPIN #2 (K)
  #0, CK_SEEN, CK_LAST, CJ_SEEN, CJ_LAST, CP_N, CP_B0, CP_B1, CP_B2, CP_B3, CP_EOP
  '  LX_N, LX_B0..LX_B3, LX_EOP   characterization: packet after the live changes and a re-issued WXPIN
  #10, LS0_SEEN, LS0_LAST, LS_SEEN, LS_LAST, LB0_SEEN, LB0_LAST, LB_SEEN, LB_LAST
  #18, LP_N, LP_B0, LP_B1, LP_B2, LP_B3, LP_EOP, LX_N, LX_B0, LX_B1, LX_B2, LX_B3, LX_EOP, DS_SEEN, DS_LAST, DB_SEEN, DB_LAST
  RECW              = 34
  CTL_LONGS         = 10                ' the control part of a record (CK..CP_EOP)

  MB_DONE           = 0
  MB_PROG           = 1
  MB_RES            = 2
  MB_POST           = MB_RES + ROUNDS * RECW     ' control after the rounds (CTL_LONGS)
  MB_LONGS          = MB_POST + CTL_LONGS

CON ' ---- Report Parameters ----
  LINE_MAX          = 400
  DEC_TOP           = 1_000_000_000
  DEC_DIGITS        = 10
  DEC_BASE          = 10
  HEX_DIGITS        = 8
  HEX_BITS          = 4
  HEX_GROUP         = 4
  HEX_LETTERS       = 10

VAR ' ---- Mailbox & Analysis State ----
  long mailbox[MB_LONGS]
  long fail_count
  byte lineBuf[LINE_MAX + 1]
  long linePos


PUB main() | engineCog, startTick
'' Run the F372 rig: check the constants, start the measuring cog, wait for its done flag, report.
''

' Local Variables:
' @local engineCog - cog id COGINIT returned (negative = no free cog)
' @local startTick - CT when the wait for the done flag began

  longfill(@mailbox, 0, MB_LONGS)
  mailbox[MB_PROG] := 0
  fail_count := 0
  linePos := 0
  say(string("=== VO-F372: USB %11011 -- does a new WRPIN on a RUNNING pair change drive / sniffer cleanly? ==="))
  ln_s(string("pair DM = P"))
  ln_u(PIN_DM)
  ln_s(string(", DP = P"))
  ln_u(PIN_DP)
  ln_s(string(" (NOTHING attached; both are driven); host, full-speed, X = "))
  ln_h(X_USB)
  ln_s(string("; "))
  ln_u(ROUNDS)
  say(string(" rounds"))
  print_predictions()
  say(string(" "))
  say(string("--- CONTROL W: configuration words, decoded into the published WRPIN fields ---"))
  check_rig_constants()
  if fail_count <> 0
    say(string("NO VERDICT: a construction control failed (see RIG FAIL lines above); the measuring cog was not started"))
  else
    engineCog := coginit(COGEXEC_NEW, @engine, @mailbox)
    if engineCog < 0
      say(string("RIG FAIL: no free cog for the measuring engine"))
      say(string("NO VERDICT: nothing was measured"))
    else
      startTick := getct()
      repeat until mailbox[MB_DONE] == MBOX_DONE or (getct() - startTick) > clkfreq * RIG_TIMEOUT_SEC
      if mailbox[MB_DONE] <> MBOX_DONE
        cogstop(engineCog)
        pinclear(PIN_DM addpins 1)
        ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: measuring cog did not report done within "))
        ln_u(RIG_TIMEOUT_SEC)
        ln_s(string(" s; it was in round "))
        ln_u(mailbox[MB_PROG])
        say(string("; the pair was cleared by cog 0"))
        say(string("NO VERDICT: the measurement did not complete"))
      else
        ln_s(string("measuring cog = "))
        ln_u(engineCog)
        say(string(" (debugger restricted to cog 0)"))
        report()
  finish()


PRI finish()
' Every terminal path ends here. pnut-term-ts ends the run when
' DEBUG_END_SESSION appears in the output (--headless or --exit-on-end-session).
'

  say(string("=== END ==="))
  debug("DEBUG_END_SESSION")
  repeat

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' line output.  Text lives in hub (string(...)), not in DEBUG data: each line
' is built in lineBuf and sent by the single debug() record in ln_out().
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI ln_c(ch)
' Append one character to the line (cut at LINE_MAX).
'
' @param ch - the character

  if linePos < LINE_MAX
    lineBuf[linePos++] := ch

PRI ln_s(pStr) | ch
' Append a zero-terminated hub string to the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

' Local Variables:
' @local ch - the character being copied

  repeat
    ch := byte[pStr++]
    if ch == 0
      quit
    ln_c(ch)

PRI ln_u(numVal) | divisor, digitVal, bStarted
' Append an unsigned decimal to the line.
'
' @param numVal - the number, read as unsigned

' Local Variables:
' @local divisor - the decimal place being printed
' @local digitVal - the digit at that place
' @local bStarted - a non-zero digit has been printed

  divisor := DEC_TOP
  bStarted := FALSE
  repeat DEC_DIGITS
    digitVal := numVal +/ divisor
    if digitVal <> 0 or bStarted or divisor == 1
      ln_c("0" + digitVal)
      bStarted := TRUE
    numVal := numVal +// divisor
    divisor /= DEC_BASE

PRI ln_h(numVal) | idx, nibble
' Append a long in hex as $XXXX_XXXX.
'
' @param numVal - the number

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - nibble index, 7 (top) .. 0
' @local nibble - the nibble value

  ln_c("$")
  repeat idx from HEX_DIGITS - 1 to 0
    nibble := (numVal >> (idx * HEX_BITS)) & $F
    if nibble < HEX_LETTERS
      ln_c("0" + nibble)
    else
      ln_c("A" + nibble - HEX_LETTERS)
    if idx == HEX_GROUP
      ln_c("_")

PRI ln_bin(numVal, digits) | idx
' Append "%" and the low digits bits of a number.
'
' @param numVal - the number
' @param digits - how many bits

' Local Variables:
' @local idx - bit index

  ln_c("%")
  repeat idx from digits - 1 to 0
    ln_c("0" + ((numVal >> idx) & 1))

PRI ln_out()
' Send the line built so far as one debug() record and start a new line.
'

  lineBuf[linePos] := 0
  debug(zstr_(@lineBuf))
  linePos := 0

PRI say(pStr)
' Append a string and send the line.
'
' @param pStr - hub address of the string

  ln_s(pStr)
  ln_out()

PRI yes_no(bFlag) : pText
' Printable YES / NO.
'
' @param bFlag - TRUE or FALSE
' @returns pText - address of "YES" or "NO"

  if bFlag
    pText := string("YES")
  else
    pText := string("NO")

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' pre-registered outcomes and construction controls
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI print_predictions()
' Print the outcomes fixed before the run.
'

  say(string("PRE-REGISTERED OUTCOMES (fixed before the run):"))
  say(string("  SNAPSHOT = settle, then 8 quiet status reads; SEEN = OR of (status AND %111): bit0 J, bit1 K, bit2 SE0"))
  say(string("  CONTROL (1): WYPIN #2 -> SEEN %010 ; WYPIN #3 -> SEEN %001 ; packet SOP,$A5,$5A,$3C,$C3 returns 4 bytes -- else RIG FAIL / NO VERDICT"))
  say(string("  DIR-cycle reference: sniffer (after WYPIN #3 = J) SEEN stable across rounds, without K and never exactly J ; back-to-drive WYPIN #2 = K -> SEEN %010 -- else RIG FAIL / INCONCLUSIVE"))
  say(string("  SNIFF_OK : live WRPIN to sniffer + WYPIN #3 gives the DIR-cycle sniffer SEEN in every round ; SNIFF_BAD : it differs in every round"))
  say(string("  BACK_OK  : live WRPIN back to drive + WYPIN #2 gives SEEN %010 (K) in every round ; BACK_BAD : it differs in every round (a pad that retained J reads %001)"))
  say(string("  PKT_OK   : packet after the live changes returns the control packet's bytes in every round ; PKT_BAD : it does not, in every round"))
  say(string("  VERDICT SURVIVES : SNIFF_OK and BACK_OK (and PKT_OK when the packet control holds) -- hardware manual / Titus / old Silicon Doc right"))
  say(string("  VERDICT BREAKS   : SNIFF_BAD or BACK_BAD or PKT_BAD -- the 'unpredictable' reading (silicon-doc-text.txt:3856) holds for this case"))
  say(string("  VERDICT INCONCLUSIVE : anything else (mixed rounds, or a gate that is not a RIG FAIL does not hold); if gate P does not hold the verdict line ends (packet arm excluded)"))
  say(string("  FALLBACK if INCONCLUSIVE because self-sense is ambiguous: a second USB pair P2/P3 with jumpers P0->P2 and P1->P3 (a separate test, not in this program)"))

PRI check_rig_constants() | baudRun
' Control W: the pair lies in the free set and is even/odd; every configuration word decodes to the
' published fields and equals its Spin2 symbol composition; the baud word equals the FRAC computation.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local baudRun - (12_000_000 FRAC clkfreq) >> 16 computed at run time

  if (PIN_DM & 1) <> 0 or PIN_DP <> PIN_DM + 1 or PAIR <> PIN_DM | (1 << 6)
    say(string("RIG FAIL: the pair is not an even/odd pair addressed as DM + one additional pin"))
    fail_count++
  if PIN_DM > PIN_MAX_FREE_LOW and (PIN_DM < 32 or PIN_DM > 46)
    say(string("RIG FAIL: DM is outside the free set (P0..P7, P32..P47)"))
    fail_count++
  check_word(string("drive   "), CFG_DRIVE, SYM_DRIVE, TT_ON)
  check_word(string("sniffer "), CFG_SNIFF, SYM_SNIFF, TT_OFF)
  baudRun := (12_000_000 frac clkfreq) >> 16
  ln_s(string("  WXPIN word "))
  ln_h(X_USB)
  ln_s(string(": D[15] host="))
  ln_u((X_USB >> 15) & 1)
  ln_s(string(" D[14] full-speed="))
  ln_u((X_USB >> 14) & 1)
  ln_s(string(" D[13:0] baud="))
  ln_u(X_USB & $3FFF)
  ln_s(string("  FRAC computation at "))
  ln_u(clkfreq)
  ln_s(string(" Hz = "))
  ln_u(baudRun)
  ln_out()
  if baudRun <> USB_BAUD or (X_USB & $3FFF) <> baudRun or ((X_USB >> 14) & 3) <> %11
    say(string("RIG FAIL: the WXPIN word does not hold host + full-speed + the computed 12 Mbps baud"))
    fail_count++

PRI check_word(pLabel, cfgWord, symWord, expTt)
' Decode one WRPIN word into its published fields, print them, and count a
' construction failure if any field or the symbol composition disagrees.
'
' @param pLabel - label string for the printed line
' @param cfgWord - the configuration word the measuring cog writes
' @param symWord - the same word composed from the Spin2 v55 symbols
' @param expTt - expected %TT

  ln_s(string("  "))
  ln_s(pLabel)
  ln_c(" ")
  ln_h(cfgWord)
  ln_s(string(": AAAA="))
  ln_bin((cfgWord >> SHIFT_AAAA) & MASK_AAAA, 4)
  ln_s(string(" BBBB="))
  ln_bin((cfgWord >> SHIFT_BBBB) & MASK_BBBB, 4)
  ln_s(string(" FFF="))
  ln_bin((cfgWord >> SHIFT_FFF) & MASK_FFF, 3)
  ln_s(string(" M="))
  ln_bin((cfgWord >> SHIFT_M) & MASK_M, 13)
  ln_s(string(" TT="))
  ln_bin((cfgWord >> SHIFT_TT) & MASK_TT, 2)
  ln_s(string(" SSSSS="))
  ln_bin((cfgWord >> SHIFT_SSSSS) & MASK_SSSSS, 5)
  ln_s(string(" bit0="))
  ln_u(cfgWord & MASK_BIT0)
  ln_s(string("  symbols="))
  ln_h(symWord)
  ln_out()
  if ((cfgWord >> SHIFT_AAAA) & MASK_AAAA) <> 0 or ((cfgWord >> SHIFT_BBBB) & MASK_BBBB) <> 0 or ((cfgWord >> SHIFT_FFF) & MASK_FFF) <> 0 or ((cfgWord >> SHIFT_M) & MASK_M) <> 0 or ((cfgWord >> SHIFT_TT) & MASK_TT) <> expTt or ((cfgWord >> SHIFT_SSSSS) & MASK_SSSSS) <> SSSSS_USB or (cfgWord & MASK_BIT0) <> 0
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: "))
    ln_s(pLabel)
    say(string(" fields differ from the expected AAAA/BBBB/FFF/M = 0, TT, SSSSS = %11011, bit0 = 0"))
    fail_count++
  if cfgWord <> symWord
    ln_s(string("RIG FAIL: "))
    ln_s(pLabel)
    ln_s(string(" word "))
    ln_h(cfgWord)
    ln_s(string(" differs from its Spin2 symbol composition "))
    ln_h(symWord)
    ln_out()
    fail_count++

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' report
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRI rec(roundIdx, slotIdx) : recVal
' One recorded long of a round.
'
' @param roundIdx - 0..ROUNDS-1
' @param slotIdx - CK_SEEN..DB_LAST
' @returns recVal - the recorded long

  recVal := mailbox[MB_RES + roundIdx * RECW + slotIdx]

PRI postrec(slotIdx) : recVal
' One recorded long of the control run after the rounds.
'
' @param slotIdx - CK_SEEN..CP_EOP
' @returns recVal - the recorded long

  recVal := mailbox[MB_POST + slotIdx]

PRI pkt_equal(roundA, roundB) : bEqual | byteIdx
' Whether the packets of two records hold the same count and bytes.
'
' @param roundA - round whose control packet (CP_*) is compared
' @param roundB - round whose live packet (LP_*) is compared
' @returns bEqual - TRUE when count and four bytes agree

' Local Variables:
' @local byteIdx - byte index

  bEqual := rec(roundA, CP_N) == rec(roundB, LP_N) and rec(roundA, CP_EOP) == rec(roundB, LP_EOP)
  repeat byteIdx from 0 to NBYTES - 1
    if rec(roundA, CP_B0 + byteIdx) <> rec(roundB, LP_B0 + byteIdx)
      bEqual := FALSE

PRI pkt_good(bytesBase, countVal) : bGood | byteIdx
' Whether a packet record holds the 4 bytes that were sent.
'
' @param bytesBase - mailbox index of the packet's first byte
' @param countVal - bytes counted
' @returns bGood - TRUE when exactly the four bytes arrived in order

' Local Variables:
' @local byteIdx - byte index

  bGood := countVal == NBYTES and mailbox[bytesBase] == TX0 and mailbox[bytesBase + 1] == TX1 and mailbox[bytesBase + 2] == TX2 and mailbox[bytesBase + 3] == TX3

PRI report() | roundIdx, bCtl, bPkt, bRef, bSniffObs, bBackObs, bSniffOk, bSniffBad, bBackOk, bBackBad, bPktOk, bPktBad
' Print the raw records, gate, decide. Single exit.
'

' Local Variables:
' @local roundIdx - round
' @local bCtl - control arm (1) holds in every round and after the rounds
' @local bPkt - control packet returns the four bytes in every round and after
' @local bRef - DIR-cycle back-to-drive snapshot is K in every round (gate R)
' @local bSniffObs - DIR-cycle sniffer snapshot stable and without K (gate O)
' @local bBackObs - DIR-cycle sniffer snapshot never exactly J (gate B)
' @local bSniffOk - live sniffer snapshot equals the DIR-cycle one in every round
' @local bSniffBad - ... differs in every round
' @local bBackOk - live back snapshot is K in every round
' @local bBackBad - ... is not K in every round
' @local bPktOk - live packet equals the control packet in every round
' @local bPktBad - ... differs in every round

  say(string(" "))
  say(string("--- RAW RECORDS per round (SEEN = OR of status AND %111 over 8 reads ; LAST = last status word) ---"))
  repeat roundIdx from 0 to ROUNDS - 1
    print_round(roundIdx)
  ln_s(string("  control after the rounds: K seen "))
  ln_bin(postrec(CK_SEEN), 3)
  ln_s(string("  J seen "))
  ln_bin(postrec(CJ_SEEN), 3)
  ln_s(string("  packet n="))
  ln_u(postrec(CP_N))
  ln_s(string(" bytes "))
  ln_h(postrec(CP_B0))
  ln_c(" ")
  ln_h(postrec(CP_B1))
  ln_c(" ")
  ln_h(postrec(CP_B2))
  ln_c(" ")
  ln_h(postrec(CP_B3))
  ln_out()
  say(string(" "))
  say(string("--- GATES ---"))
  bCtl := TRUE
  bPkt := pkt_good(MB_POST + CP_B0, postrec(CP_N))
  if postrec(CK_SEEN) <> SEEN_K or postrec(CJ_SEEN) <> SEEN_J
    bCtl := FALSE
  repeat roundIdx from 0 to ROUNDS - 1
    if rec(roundIdx, CK_SEEN) <> SEEN_K or rec(roundIdx, CJ_SEEN) <> SEEN_J
      bCtl := FALSE
    if pkt_good(MB_RES + roundIdx * RECW + CP_B0, rec(roundIdx, CP_N)) == FALSE
      bPkt := FALSE
  ln_s(string("  K  control (1) K=%010 and J=%001 in every round and after: "))
  ln_s(yes_no(bCtl))
  ln_out()
  if bCtl == FALSE
    say(string("RIG FAIL: the control arm (1) does not show K / J on the pair's own receiver -- the pair is not driving, or self-sense does not work (the fallback is then needed: a second pair P2/P3 with jumpers P0->P2 and P1->P3, a separate test)"))
    fail_count++
  bRef := TRUE
  bSniffObs := TRUE
  bBackObs := TRUE
  repeat roundIdx from 0 to ROUNDS - 1
    if rec(roundIdx, DB_SEEN) <> SEEN_K
      bRef := FALSE
    if rec(roundIdx, DS_SEEN) <> rec(0, DS_SEEN) or (rec(roundIdx, DS_SEEN) & SEEN_K) <> 0
      bSniffObs := FALSE
    if rec(roundIdx, DS_SEEN) == SEEN_J
      bBackObs := FALSE
  ln_s(string("  R  DIR-cycle back-to-drive (WYPIN #2 = K) gives K in every round: "))
  ln_s(yes_no(bRef))
  ln_out()
  if bRef == FALSE
    say(string("RIG FAIL: the documented reconfigure (DIRL, WRPIN, WXPIN, DIRH) does not restore the drive"))
    fail_count++
  ln_s(string("  O  DIR-cycle sniffer snapshot identical in every round and without K: "))
  ln_s(yes_no(bSniffObs))
  ln_s(string("  (round 0 SEEN "))
  ln_bin(rec(0, DS_SEEN), 3)
  ln_c(")")
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("  B  DIR-cycle sniffer snapshot never exactly J (%001) in any round (else the back arm is INCONCLUSIVE): "))
  ln_s(yes_no(bBackObs))
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("  P  control packet returned SOP-framed bytes $A5 $5A $3C $C3 in every round and after: "))
  ln_s(yes_no(bPkt))
  ln_out()
  say(string(" "))
  if fail_count <> 0
    say(string("NO VERDICT: a gating control failed (see RIG FAIL lines above); the records are printed for diagnosis only"))
  else
    bSniffOk := TRUE
    bSniffBad := TRUE
    bBackOk := TRUE
    bBackBad := TRUE
    bPktOk := TRUE
    bPktBad := TRUE
    repeat roundIdx from 0 to ROUNDS - 1
      if rec(roundIdx, LS_SEEN) == rec(roundIdx, DS_SEEN)
        bSniffBad := FALSE
      else
        bSniffOk := FALSE
      if rec(roundIdx, LB_SEEN) == SEEN_K
        bBackBad := FALSE
      else
        bBackOk := FALSE
      if pkt_equal(roundIdx, roundIdx)
        bPktBad := FALSE
      else
        bPktOk := FALSE
    ln_s(string("  SNIFF_OK "))
    ln_s(yes_no(bSniffOk))
    ln_s(string("  SNIFF_BAD "))
    ln_s(yes_no(bSniffBad))
    ln_s(string("   BACK_OK "))
    ln_s(yes_no(bBackOk))
    ln_s(string("  BACK_BAD "))
    ln_s(yes_no(bBackBad))
    ln_s(string("   PKT_OK "))
    ln_s(yes_no(bPktOk))
    ln_s(string("  PKT_BAD "))
    ln_s(yes_no(bPktBad))
    ln_out()
    if bPkt == FALSE
      say(string("  (gate P does not hold: the packet arm is characterization only and is left out of the verdict)"))
      bPktOk := TRUE
      bPktBad := FALSE
    if bBackObs == FALSE
      say(string("  (gate B does not hold: the DIR-cycle sniffer reads exactly J, so the back-to-drive arm is INCONCLUSIVE and is left out)"))
      bBackOk := FALSE
      bBackBad := FALSE
    if bSniffObs == FALSE
      ln_s(string("VERDICT VO-F372: INCONCLUSIVE - the DIR-cycle sniffer snapshot is not stable or still shows K: drive and sniffer cannot be told apart in this rig (records above); fallback: a second pair with jumpers P0->P2, P1->P3"))
      excl_note(bPkt)
      ln_out()
    elseif bSniffBad or bBackBad or bPktBad
      ln_s(string("VERDICT VO-F372: BREAKS - the live WRPIN differs from the reset-based reconfigure in every round for at least one of: sniffer snapshot, back-to-drive snapshot, packet"))
      excl_note(bPkt)
      ln_out()
      say(string("  a new WRPIN on a running USB pair does NOT reproduce the DIR-cycle result: the 'without resetting the smart pin' sentence does not hold here"))
    elseif bSniffOk and bBackOk and bPktOk
      ln_s(string("VERDICT VO-F372: SURVIVES - the live WRPIN reproduces the DIR-cycle result in every round, and the pair carries a packet afterwards"))
      excl_note(bPkt)
      ln_out()
      say(string("  a new WRPIN %0_11011_0 / %1_11011_0 on a running USB pair works without a reset (hardware manual / Titus / old Silicon Doc right)"))
    else
      ln_s(string("VERDICT VO-F372: INCONCLUSIVE - rounds disagree, or one live snapshot matches in some rounds only, or the back arm is not observable (records above); fallback: a second pair with jumpers P0->P2, P1->P3"))
      excl_note(bPkt)
      ln_out()

PRI excl_note(bPktGate)
' Append " (packet arm excluded)" to the line being built when gate P failed (the packet arm is then not in the verdict).
'
' @param bPktGate - gate P: the control packet returned the four bytes in every round

  if bPktGate == FALSE
    ln_s(string(" (packet arm excluded)"))

PRI print_round(roundIdx)
' Print one round's record as a few lines.
'
' @param roundIdx - 0..ROUNDS-1

  ln_s(string("  round "))
  ln_u(roundIdx + 1)
  ln_s(string(" control: K "))
  ln_bin(rec(roundIdx, CK_SEEN), 3)
  ln_s(string(" J "))
  ln_bin(rec(roundIdx, CJ_SEEN), 3)
  ln_s(string(" packet n="))
  ln_u(rec(roundIdx, CP_N))
  ln_s(string(" bytes "))
  ln_h(rec(roundIdx, CP_B0))
  ln_c(" ")
  ln_h(rec(roundIdx, CP_B1))
  ln_c(" ")
  ln_h(rec(roundIdx, CP_B2))
  ln_c(" ")
  ln_h(rec(roundIdx, CP_B3))
  ln_s(string(" eop "))
  ln_u(rec(roundIdx, CP_EOP))
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("           live sniffer: after WRPIN "))
  ln_bin(rec(roundIdx, LS0_SEEN), 3)
  ln_s(string(" after WYPIN #3 (J) "))
  ln_bin(rec(roundIdx, LS_SEEN), 3)
  ln_s(string(" (last "))
  ln_h(rec(roundIdx, LS_LAST))
  ln_s(string(")   live back: after WRPIN "))
  ln_bin(rec(roundIdx, LB0_SEEN), 3)
  ln_s(string(" after WYPIN #2 (K) "))
  ln_bin(rec(roundIdx, LB_SEEN), 3)
  ln_s(string(" (last "))
  ln_h(rec(roundIdx, LB_LAST))
  ln_c(")")
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("           live packet n="))
  ln_u(rec(roundIdx, LP_N))
  ln_s(string(" bytes "))
  ln_h(rec(roundIdx, LP_B0))
  ln_c(" ")
  ln_h(rec(roundIdx, LP_B1))
  ln_c(" ")
  ln_h(rec(roundIdx, LP_B2))
  ln_c(" ")
  ln_h(rec(roundIdx, LP_B3))
  ln_s(string(" eop "))
  ln_u(rec(roundIdx, LP_EOP))
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("           characterization, packet again after WXPIN re-issued: n="))
  ln_u(rec(roundIdx, LX_N))
  ln_s(string(" bytes "))
  ln_h(rec(roundIdx, LX_B0))
  ln_c(" ")
  ln_h(rec(roundIdx, LX_B1))
  ln_c(" ")
  ln_h(rec(roundIdx, LX_B2))
  ln_c(" ")
  ln_h(rec(roundIdx, LX_B3))
  ln_s(string(" eop "))
  ln_u(rec(roundIdx, LX_EOP))
  ln_out()
  ln_s(string("           DIR-cycle: sniffer (J written) "))
  ln_bin(rec(roundIdx, DS_SEEN), 3)
  ln_s(string(" (last "))
  ln_h(rec(roundIdx, DS_LAST))
  ln_s(string(")  back (K written) "))
  ln_bin(rec(roundIdx, DB_SEEN), 3)
  ln_s(string(" (last "))
  ln_h(rec(roundIdx, DB_LAST))
  ln_c(")")
  ln_out()

{ MEASURING ENGINE -- runs in its own cog; the ONLY code that touches the pair.
  No debug() here (DEBUG_COGS excludes this cog anyway). PTRA = @mailbox on entry.
  respt_ walks the mailbox in the order the CK_SEEN..DB_LAST constants list (RECW longs
  per round), then the CTL_LONGS of the control run after the rounds.
}
DAT             org     0        ' ---- Measuring Engine ----
engine          mov     mb_, ptra
                mov     respt_, mb_
                add     respt_, #MB_RES * 4
                mov     progp_, mb_
                add     progp_, #MB_PROG * 4
                mov     rnd_, #ROUNDS
                mov     roundno_, #0

.round          add     roundno_, #1
                wrlong  roundno_, progp_

                ' ---- LIVE ARM ----
                mov     cfg_, cfg_drive_
                call    #usb_start
                call    #control_arm            ' (1) K, J, packet                      -> CK, CJ, CP
                wrpin   cfg_sniff_, #PAIR       ' (2) live to sniffer, DIR high, no DIR change, no WXPIN
                call    #snap                   '     after WRPIN, no write             -> LS0
                wypin   #3, #PAIR               '     J (a pad that retains J is then not mistaken for a K)
                call    #snap                   '     after WYPIN #3                    -> LS
                wrpin   cfg_drive_, #PAIR       ' (3) live back to drive
                call    #snap                   '     after WRPIN, no write             -> LB0
                wypin   #2, #PAIR               '     K: only the drive can produce it after the J above
                call    #snap                   '     after WYPIN #2                    -> LB
                wypin   #3, #PAIR               '     back to J (idle) so the packet starts from the same state as the control's
                waitx   ##SETTLE_CLK
                call    #packet                 ' (4) packet after the live changes     -> LP
                wxpin   x_usb_, #PIN_DM         '     characterization: WXPIN re-issued on the running pair
                waitx   ##START_CLK
                call    #packet                 '     packet again                      -> LX

                ' ---- DIR-CYCLE ARM (the reset-based reference) ----
                mov     cfg_, cfg_drive_
                call    #usb_start              ' the documented start again
                mov     cfg_, cfg_sniff_
                call    #usb_cycle              ' DIRL, WRPIN sniffer, WXPIN, DIRH
                wypin   #3, #PAIR               ' J, as in the live arm
                call    #snap                   '                                       -> DS
                mov     cfg_, cfg_drive_
                call    #usb_cycle              ' DIRL, WRPIN drive, WXPIN, DIRH
                wypin   #2, #PAIR               ' K, as in the live arm
                call    #snap                   '                                       -> DB
                djnz    rnd_, #.round

                ' ---- control after the rounds ----
                mov     cfg_, cfg_drive_
                call    #usb_start
                call    #control_arm            ' -> the post record (CTL_LONGS)

                call    #usb_off                ' leave P0 / P1 safe
                wrlong  #MBOX_DONE, ptra        ' done -- always the last write
                cogid   self_id_
                cogstop self_id_

' All of it off: pair DIR low, smart pin off, OUT low.
usb_off         dirl    #PAIR
                wrpin   #0, #PAIR
                outl    #PAIR
                waitx   #100
                ret

' The documented start (silicon-doc-text.txt:4593): reset, WRPIN cfg_ on both pins, WXPIN on DM, DIRH both.
usb_start       call    #usb_off
usb_cycle       dirl    #PAIR                   ' (usb_cycle: DIRL, WRPIN new word, WXPIN, DIRH -- no WRPIN #0)
                wrpin   cfg_, #PAIR
                wxpin   x_usb_, #PIN_DM
                dirh    #PAIR
                waitx   ##START_CLK
                ret

' (1) CONTROL: WYPIN K, snapshot; WYPIN J, snapshot; packet.  Writes CTL_LONGS longs.
control_arm     wypin   #2, #PAIR
                call    #snap
                wypin   #3, #PAIR
                call    #snap
                call    #packet
                ret

' Snapshot: settle, then SAMPLES quiet reads of the lower pin's status word.
' Writes two longs: SEEN (OR of status AND %111), LAST (last status word).
snap            waitx   ##SETTLE_CLK
                mov     seen_, #0
                mov     si_, #SAMPLES
.s              rqpin   st_, #PIN_DM
                mov     tg_, st_
                and     tg_, #%111
                or      seen_, tg_
                waitx   #SPACE_CLK
                djnz    si_, #.s
                mov     val_, seen_
                call    #put
                mov     val_, st_
                call    #put
                ret

' Framed packet: SOP and the four data bytes written as the FIFO has room (DP's IN high),
' while the lower pin's status is polled; each toggle of the byte-toggle bit (bit 7), once SOP-in
' (bit 4) has been seen, is a received byte.  Writes six longs: n, four bytes, EOP-in.
packet          mov     nrx_, #0
                mov     txi_, #0
                mov     insop_, #0
                mov     prevtg_, #0
                mov     rx0_, nobyte_
                mov     rx1_, nobyte_
                mov     rx2_, nobyte_
                mov     rx3_, nobyte_
                getct   tp0_
.loop           cmp     txi_, #NTX              wc      ' C = 1 while values remain to write
        if_nc   jmp     #.rx
                testp   #PIN_DP                 wc      ' DP IN high = the output FIFO has room
        if_nc   jmp     #.rx
                alts    txi_, #txdata_                  ' S of the next instruction = txdata_ + txi_
                mov     b_, 0-0
                wypin   b_, #PAIR                       ' writes DM and acknowledges DP
                add     txi_, #1
.rx             rqpin   st_, #PIN_DM
                mov     tg_, st_
                and     tg_, #$80
                testb   st_, #4                 wc      ' SOP in
                cmp     insop_, #0              wz
        if_z_and_c mov  insop_, #1
        if_z_and_c mov  prevtg_, tg_
        if_z    jmp     #.chk                           ' not inside a packet yet
                cmp     tg_, prevtg_            wz
        if_z    jmp     #.chk                           ' no new byte
                mov     prevtg_, tg_
                mov     b_, st_
                shr     b_, #8
                and     b_, #$FF
                cmp     nrx_, #NBYTES           wc
        if_c    altd    nrx_, #rx0_
        if_c    mov     0-0, b_
                add     nrx_, #1
.chk            cmp     txi_, #NTX              wz
        if_nz   jmp     #.tmo
                cmp     nrx_, #NBYTES           wc
        if_c    jmp     #.tmo
                testb   st_, #5                 wc      ' EOP in
        if_c    jmp     #.done
.tmo            getct   tp1_
                sub     tp1_, tp0_
                cmp     tp1_, ##PKT_TIMEOUT     wc
        if_c    jmp     #.loop
.done           testb   st_, #5                 wc
        if_c    mov     eop_, #1
        if_nc   mov     eop_, #0
                mov     val_, nrx_
                call    #put
                mov     val_, rx0_
                call    #put
                mov     val_, rx1_
                call    #put
                mov     val_, rx2_
                call    #put
                mov     val_, rx3_
                call    #put
                mov     val_, eop_
                call    #put
                waitx   ##SETTLE_CLK
                ret

put             wrlong  val_, respt_
                add     respt_, #4
                ret

cfg_drive_      long    CFG_DRIVE
cfg_sniff_      long    CFG_SNIFF
x_usb_          long    X_USB
nobyte_         long    NO_BYTE
txdata_         long    $80, TX0, TX1, TX2, TX3     ' SOP, then the data bytes (NTX longs)

mb_             res     1
respt_          res     1
progp_          res     1
rnd_            res     1
roundno_        res     1
cfg_            res     1
seen_           res     1
si_             res     1
st_             res     1
tg_             res     1
val_            res     1
nrx_            res     1
txi_            res     1
insop_          res     1
prevtg_         res     1
rx0_            res     1                       ' the four received bytes, consecutive
rx1_            res     1
rx2_            res     1
rx3_            res     1
b_              res     1
eop_            res     1
tp0_            res     1
tp1_            res     1
self_id_        res     1

